    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionAddLink">Add link</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionAddLinkDescription">Since UVL has platform specific pages for each game and the matched games may be false flags, you can set up how links should be added when importing bulk data based on that.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionAuthentication">Authentication</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionAuthenticationDescription">To be able to use the bulk import feature you need to have an account in UVL and be logged in, because only logged in users can access the pages listing all games for a tag. If you don't want to use the bulk import feature, you can skip authentication.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionDescriptionToUse">Description to use</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionDescriptionToUseDescription">Select which type of description to use for the metadata. The other one will be used as a fallback. If both are to be used, they will be separated by a horizontal line.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionDisplayTopPanelButton">Display top panel button for bulk import</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionDisplayTopPanelButtonDescription">If enabled, a button will be displayed in the top panel for bulk importing metadata. You can also access the bulk import via the extensions menu.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionLastRefresh">Last refresh:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionLastRefreshDescription">To import tags from UVL you need to refresh them using this button at least once. I recommend to refresh them once in a while to keep the metadata up to date, but they usually don't change very often.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionOnlyUseFirstDescription">Only use first description</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionOnlyUseFirstDescriptionDescription">UVL can have several descriptions for the same game. If enabled, only the first description of the selected type will be used. Otherwise all will be fetched and separated by a horizontal line.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionRatingToUse">Critic score to use</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsCaptionRatingToUseDescription">Select which rating to use for the metadata. The median and average scores are calculated from the list of reviews on the UVL website.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsDescriptionToUseBoth">Both</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsDescriptionToUseDescription">Description</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsDescriptionToUseOfficialDescription">Official Description</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsRatingAverage">Average</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsRatingMedian">Median</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsSectionBulkImport">Bulk Import</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsSectionBulkImportDescription">Using the bulk import feature you can import UVL tags for multiple games at once. You can access it via the menu option in the extensions menu or optionally a top panel button configured below.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsSectionGeneral">General</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsSectionTags">Tags</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCUVLMetadataSettingsSectionTagsDescription">Here you can define which tag categories you want to add as tags, features or genres and specify a prefix for it. Tags of the type &quot;series&quot; will always be added to the series field and won't have a prefix.</sys:String>
